{"component_id_namespace":"ec077a53-0b40-5f21-b1fe-a62094d2476b","component_schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","components":[{"attributes":{"code":"TMC","legacy_node_id":"ks-topeka:tmc:14.55.230","page_type":"section"},"citation":"14.55.230","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/14.55.230","content_hash":"587e24cda2e87df6a1a2a750c92e2ddcac20902c890111e44648ea5332d945d7","heading":"IRC Table R301.2(1).","ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":null,"schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:14.55.230:section","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/14.55.230","text":"Table R301.2(1) is hereby deleted in its entirety and the following table shall be substituted therefor:\nGround Snow Load | Wind Design | Seismic Design Category f | Subject To Damage From | Winter Design Temp e | Ice Barrier Underlayment Required h | Flood Hazards g | Air Freezing Index i | Mean Annual Temp j\nSpeed d (mph) | Topographic Effects k | Weathering a | Frost Line Depth b | Termite c\n20 | 114 | NO | A | Severe | 36\" | Moderate to Heavy | 4 | NO | Oct 23, 1971, entry into National Flood Insurance Program. Current maps dated September 29, 2011, entitled “Flood Insurance Rate Map for Shawnee County KS” | 1000 | 54.3\nIRC TABLE R301.2(1)\nCLIMATIC AND GEOGRAPHIC DESIGN CRITERIA\nGround Snow Load\nWind Design\nSeismic Design Category f\nSubject To Damage From\nWinter Design Temp e\nIce Barrier Underlayment Required h\nFlood Hazards g\nAir Freezing Index i\nMean Annual Temp j\nSpeed d (mph)\nTopographic Effects k\nWeathering a\nFrost Line Depth b\nTermite c\n20\n114\nNO\nA\nSevere\n36\"\nModerate to Heavy\n4\nNO\nOct 23, 1971, entry into National Flood Insurance Program. Current maps dated September 29, 2011, entitled “Flood Insurance Rate Map for Shawnee County KS”\n1000\n54.3\nFor SI: 1 pound per square foot = 0.0479 kN/m 2 , 1 mile = 1.609km/h.\na Weathering may require a higher strength concrete or grade of masonry than necessary to satisfy the structural requirements of this code. The weathering column shall be filled in with the weathering index (i.e., “negligible,” “moderate” or “severe”) for concrete as determined from the Weathering Probability Map [Figure R301.2(3)]. The grade of masonry units shall be determined from ASTM C 34, C 55, C 62, C 73, C 90, C 129, C 145, C 216 or C 652.\nb The frost line depth may require deeper footings than indicated in Figure R403.1(1). The jurisdiction shall fill in the frost line depth column with the minimum depth of footing below finish grade.\nc The jurisdiction shall fill in this part of the table to indicate the need for protection depending on whether there has been a history of local subterranean termite damage.\nd The jurisdiction shall fill in this part of the table with the wind speed from the basic wind speed map [Figure R301.2(4)]. Wind exposure category shall be determined on site-specific basis in accordance with Section R301.2.1.4.\ne The outdoor design dry-bulb temperature shall be selected from the columns of 97 1/2-percent values for winter from Appendix D of the International Plumbing Code. Deviations from the Appendix D temperatures shall be permitted to reflect local climates or local weather experience as determined by the building official.\nf The jurisdiction shall fill in this part of the table with the Seismic Design Category determined from Section R301.2.2.1.\ng The jurisdiction shall fill in this part of the table with (a) the date of the jurisdiction’s entry into the National Flood Insurance Program (date of adoption of the first code or ordinance for management of flood hazard areas), (b) the date(s) of the Flood Insurance Study and (c) the panel numbers and dates of all currently effective FIRMs and FBFMs or other flood hazard map adopted by the authority having jurisdiction, as amended.\nh In accordance with Sections R905.2.7.1, R905.4.3.1, R905.5.3.1, R905.6.3.1, R905.7.3.1 and R905.8.3.1, where there has been a history of local damage from the effects of ice damming, the jurisdiction shall fill in this part of the table with “YES.” Otherwise, the jurisdiction shall fill in this part of the table with “NO.”\ni The jurisdiction shall fill in this part of the table with the 100-year return period air freezing index (BF-days) from Figure R403.3(2) or from the 100-year (99%) value on the National Climatic Data Center data table “Air Freezing Index-USA Method (Base 32° Fahrenheit)” at www.ncdc.noaa.gov/fpsf.html.\nj The jurisdiction shall fill in this part of the table with the mean annual temperature from the National Climatic Data Center data table “Air Freezing Index-USA Method (Base 32° Fahrenheit)” at www.ncdc.noaa.gov/fpsf.html.\nk In accordance with Section R301.2.1.5, where there is local historical data documenting structural damage to buildings due to topographic wind speed-up effects, the jurisdiction shall fill in this part of the table with “YES.” Otherwise, the jurisdiction shall indicate “NO” in this part of the table.\n(Ord. 20467 § 9, 12-5-23.)","type":"section","workbench_component_id":"2a85db06-9f93-5bd6-9ed7-bcec9fb37662"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"14.55.230","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/14.55.230","content_hash":"2d676447c3a013da7ba65dca4c6c3fc99cf853fe6f512e7d3e5294b3dbc595e1","heading":null,"ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:14.55.230:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:14.55.230:block:0","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/14.55.230","text":"Table R301.2(1) is hereby deleted in its entirety and the following table shall be substituted therefor:","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"acdcf5e0-5a5a-5680-a609-d4f983b3d120"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"table"},"citation":"14.55.230","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/14.55.230","content_hash":"77de38